  "details": "What if VRChat revamped its AFK system to provide a more accurate detection mechanism? Currently, I encounter issues with the system falsely marking me as AFK even when I'm actively engaged with my desktop or the Steam menu. This situation forces me to disable AFK detection altogether, which means missing out on the opportunity to showcase cool AFK animations for my avatars.\n\nTo address this problem effectively, I propose that VRChat adopts a more reliable method for detecting AFK status. Rather than relying on whether the Steam menu is open or closed, the system should utilize the headset's sensors to determine activity levels. By monitoring movement updates or lack thereof within a specified timeframe, the AFK system could accurately identify when a user is genuinely idle.\n\nThis improvement would enable users like myself to freely navigate the Steam menu, making necessary adjustments to optimize our VR experience without triggering unnecessary AFK animations. This way, we can comfortably engage with the desktop environment while avoiding any disruptions to our interactions within VRChat, such as unintentionally smacking others with our AFK animations while participating in a cuddle pile.\n\nImplementing this suggested approach would enhance the overall user experience by ensuring that AFK detection aligns more closely with user behavior, allowing for seamless navigation and customization without sacrificing the ability to showcase creative AFK animations.",
